":"GVA (balanced, total)","value":2790000.0,"year":"2023","kind":"money"},{"label":"GVA per head","value":23376,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"GDP per head","value":27305,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2430.23,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":215.99,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":{"summary":"Chorley ended 2025/26 with \u00a383.6m of gross debt (\u00a363.0m PWLB plus \u00a320m of short-term loans from other local authorities) against a \u00a3110.6m capital financing requirement and year-end investments of just \u00a311.2m. Debt actually fell \u00a34.0m in the year \u2014 no new long-term PWLB was taken and capital spending came in at \u00a310.1m against a \u00a346.8m original estimate \u2014 but financing costs still consumed 19.07% of the net revenue stream, 1.38 points above budget and an unusually heavy load for a shire district. The \u00a320m of local-authority loans (about a quarter of the debt book) must be refinanced within the year against thin cash, with the council \u00a327m internally borrowed. All borrowing limits were complied with throughout the year.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Treasury Management Outturn Report 2025/26","as_of_url":"https://chorley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s199142/Treasury Management Outturn Report 202526 Committee Report Template.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-07-22","signals":[{"code":"debt-servicing-rising","headline":"Financing costs took 19.07% of Chorley's net revenue stream in 2025/26, vs 17.69% estimated (+1.38pp)","why":"Nearly a fifth of the council's revenue base is committed to capital financing before any service is delivered."},{"code":"refinancing-risk","headline":"\u00a320m of short-term local-authority loans (24% of \u00a383.6m gross debt) fall due within 12 months, against year-end investments of \u00a311.2m","why":"Rollover of a quarter of the debt book depends on the inter-authority market in a year when neighbouring councils report that market thinning."},{"code":"debt-reducing","headline":"Gross debt fell \u00a33.96m to \u00a383.59m in 2025/26 (CFR down \u00a31.1m to \u00a3110.6m); no new long-term PWLB borrowing taken","why":"The direction of travel is contained \u2014 scheduled repayments plus \u00a336.7m of capital slippage kept the borrowing need down."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a3110,610k closing (opening \u00a3111,697k; original estimate \u00a3120,766k)","as_at":"31/3/26","page":4},{"name":"borrowing","value":"gross debt \u00a383,593k including \u00a320m short-term borrowing from other local authorities; fell \u00a33,960k in year","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":5},{"name":"pwlb portfolio","value":"\u00a362,987k PWLB loans at 1.32%-4.34%, maturities out to 2072; external borrowing total \u00a382,987k","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":10},{"name":"internal borrowing","value":"\u00a327,017k under-borrowing (Table 4; Table 6 states \u00a328,050k)","as_at":"31/3/26","page":5},{"name":"investments","value":"\u00a311,159k at year end; core funds/working balances \u00a339,209k","as_at":"31/3/26","page":6},{"name":"investment income","value":"\u00a3750k earned on \u00a314,206k average daily balance, 3.29% average yield","as_at":"2025/26","page":7},{"name":"maturity under 12m","value":"\u00a320m local-authority loans borrowed for less than 1 year (24% of gross debt)","as_at":"31 March 2026","page":5},{"name":"financing costs to net revenue","value":"19.07% actual vs 17.69% estimate (+1.38pp variance)","as_at":"2025/26","page":6},{"name":"authorised limit","value":"\u00a3132.843m (operational boundary \u00a3120.766m); actual gross debt \u00a383.593m \u2014 complied throughout","as_at":"2025/26","page":5},{"name":"capital expenditure","value":"\u00a310,134k actual vs \u00a346,837k estimate; net financing need for year \u00a3924k vs \u00a39,844k estimate","as_at":"2025/26","page":3}],"commercial":null,"tms_components":null},"compliance":null