this indicates less headroom for managing revenue volatility.","iso":"2026-07-22","paper_title":"Treasury Management Outturn Report 2025/26 Committee Report Template","paper_url":"https://chorley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s199142/199142.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Working balances came in materially below the mid-year revised forecast","lead":"Working balances are the buffer against unexpected costs or revenue shortfalls. A \u00a312.9m variance on a revised estimate signals the council could not maintain expected liquidity, which matters to lenders assessing financial resilience.","iso":"2026-07-22","paper_title":"Treasury Management Outturn Report 2025/26 Committee Report Template","paper_url":"https://chorley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s199142/199142.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Major local government reorganisation scheduled for 2028 \u2014 councils transitioning from two-tier to new structure","lead":"Major structural reorganisation creates uncertainty and diverts senior management capacity away from current operations. It presents a material governance risk period with potential for control gaps as responsibilities shift between organisations.","iso":"2026-05-27","paper_title":"Appendix A Draft Annual Governance Statement","paper_url":"https://chorley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s196900/196900.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Treasury Management Outturn Report 2025/26 Committee Report Template","paper_url":"https://chorley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s199142/199142.pdf","headline":"Financing costs consumed a higher proportion of revenue than budgeted","detail":"The ratio of financing costs to net revenue stream came in at 19.07% against an estimate of 17.69%, a 1.38 percentage point increase. This means debt service is taking a larger share of the council's available revenue than expected.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A rising financing cost ratio reduces the council's flexibility to respond to other pressures and increases the structural cost of its existing debt. For a lender, this indicates less headroom for managing revenue volatility.","figures":"Actual 19.07%, estimate 17.69%, variance 1.38%","quote":"Ratio 17.69% 19.07% 1.38%","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-22","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Treasury Management Outturn Report 2025/26 Committee Report Template","paper_url":"https://chorley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s199142/199142.pdf","headline":"Working balances came in materially below the mid-year revised forecast","detail":"Actual core funds of \u00a339.209m fell significantly short of the revised estimate of \u00a352.138m, a shortfall of \u00a312.929m (25% below revised). This indicates the council's cash position tightened unexpectedly during the year and suggests either unplanned spending or lower-than-expected income.","category":"reserves","matters":"Working balances are the buffer against unexpected costs or revenue shortfalls. A \u00a312.9m variance on a revised estimate signals the council could not maintain expected liquidity, which matters to lenders assessing financial resilience.","figures":"Core Funds / Working Balances actual \u00a339,209k, revised estimate \u00a352,138k, variance (\u00a312,929k)","quote":"Core Funds / Working Balances (42,387) (52,138) (39,209) 12,929","material":true},{"iso":"2026-05-27","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A Draft Annual Governance Statement","paper_url":"https://chorley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s196900/196900.pdf","headline":"Major local government reorganisation scheduled for 2028 \u2014 councils transitioning from two-tier to new structure","detail":"The Government plans to reconfigure local authority structures, moving away from the two-tier system. Lancashire, where Chorley sits, is included in this reorganisation. The council is actively engaged in programme arrangements to support transition to new organisations from 2028, with a March 2027 deadline for maintaining robust governance during this transition.","category":"governance","matters":"Major structural reorganisation creates uncertainty and diverts senior management capacity away from current operations. It presents a material governance risk period with potential for control gaps as responsibilities shift between organisations.","figures":"Transition to complete by 2028","quote":"The Government has set out plans to move away from the current two-tier system of district and county councils and this includes Lancashire.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-05-27","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A Draft Annual Governance Statement","paper_url":"https://chorley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s196900/196900.pdf","headline":"Data Protection compliance audit undertaken by external specialist \u2014 indicating previous gaps","detail":"An external specialist company has been commissioned to audit GDPR and Data Protection compliance. The audit is expected to identify gaps and issue recommendations. This item was carried forward from the previous year's improvement actions, indicating compliance concerns were not fully resolved.","category":"audit","matters":"GDPR compliance failures can result in regulatory penalties and reputational damage. The need for external specialist audit suggests internal capability or compliance gaps.","figures":"None provided","quote":"An audit is being undertaken by an external company who are specialist in Data Protection. The audit will identify any gaps and issue recommendations if required.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-05-27","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A Draft Annual Governance Statement","paper_url":"https://chorley.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s196900/196900.pdf","headline":"External audit continues to issue recommendations \u2014 5 new recommendations from 2024/25 audit","detail":"The 2024/25 external audit (concluded November 2025) continued to make 5 recommendations for improvements. The 11 recommendations from the prior year audit were either completed or mitigated to the extent currently possible, but the persistence of new issues indicates ongoing audit concerns.","category":"audit","matters":"Continuing external audit recommendations indicate that previously identified issues are not fully resolved and new control issues are emerging.","figures":"5 recommendations in 2024/25 audit; 11 carried forward from prior year","quote":"The most recent review undertaken (which is for the period 2024/25 concluded in November 2025) whilst continuing to make 5 recommendations for improvements","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-22"},"name":"Chorley","findings_total":35,"news_drafts_total":3}}